Imports:
  - Types:
      - Exchange
    From: freqtrade/exchange

Usages:
  extension_point: |
    To add a new pairlist/filter, subclass `IPairList`, implement short_desc and either
    _validate_pair (filter-position handlers) or gen_pairlist (generator-position handlers,
    must also set needstickers True if it needs ticker data), then register the class name in
    the user's pairlists config list. PairListResolver (in freqtrade/resolvers) is what
    dynamically loads the named class at runtime — this cell only defines the contract.

Annotations: |
  This cell is freqtrade's pair-selection extension point: a chain-of-responsibility of
  `IPairList` handlers, each either generating or filtering the tradeable pair whitelist.

  Use `extension_point` to implement a new handler.

---

"IPairList(exchange: Exchange, pairlistmanager: Any, config: dict[str, Any], pairlistconfig: dict[str, Any], pairlist_pos: int)":
  location: IPairList.py
  annotations: |
    Abstract base for one stage of the pairlist chain (whitelist generation or filtering).

    `pairlistmanager`: the owning manager (left untyped here to avoid a cell import cycle with
    the freqtrade/plugins manager cell); handlers may call back into it for whitelist state
    `pairlist_pos`: this handler's position in the configured chain (0 = first/generator stage)
  properties:
    "name -> str": |
      Class name of the handler, used in logs and API responses.
    "needstickers -> bool": |
      True if this handler requires ticker data to be fetched before filter_pairlist runs.
  methods:
    "description() -> text:str": |
      One-line human description of what this handler does, shown in /pairlists output.

      Constraints:
      - Abstract: every concrete handler must override this
    "short_desc() -> text:str": |
      Instance-level one-line description including this handler's configured parameters.

      Constraints:
      - Abstract: every concrete handler must override this
    "gen_pairlist(tickers: dict[str, Any]) -> pairlist:list[str]": |
      Produce the initial whitelist (only meaningful for position-0/generator handlers).

      `tickers`: current tickers, present only if needstickers is True
      `pairlist`: generated pair list

      Constraints:
      - Base implementation raises OperationalException; override only in generator handlers
    "filter_pairlist(pairlist: list[str], tickers: dict[str, Any]) -> pairlist:list[str]": |
      Apply this handler's filtering rule to an incoming whitelist.

      `pairlist`: whitelist as produced by the previous handler in the chain
      `tickers`: current tickers, present only if needstickers is True

      Algorithm:
      1. For each pair in `pairlist`, call _validate_pair with that pair's ticker
      2. Keep only pairs for which _validate_pair returned True
    "_validate_pair(pair: str, ticker: dict[str, Any] | None) -> keep:bool": |
      Decide whether one `pair` survives this filter.

      Constraints:
      - Override point for filter-position handlers; base raises NotImplementedError
    "verify_blacklist(pairlist: list[str], logmethod: Any) -> pairlist:list[str]": |
      Remove any blacklisted pairs from `pairlist`, logging removals via `logmethod`.
    "verify_whitelist(pairlist: list[str], logmethod: Any, keep_invalid: bool) -> pairlist:list[str]": |
      Remove pairs from `pairlist` that are not currently tradeable on exchange.

"IPairList::VolumePairList()":
  location: VolumePairList.py
  annotations: |
    Generator-position handler that whitelists the top-N pairs by traded volume. One of roughly
    15 concrete handlers in this cell; see `extension_point`.

"expand_pairlist(wildcardpl: list[str], available_pairs: list[str], keep_invalid: bool) -> pairlist:list[str]":
  location: pairlist_helpers.py
  annotations: |
    Expand a config pair list that may contain regex wildcards (e.g. ".*/USDT") into the
    concrete subset of `available_pairs` that match.

    `keep_invalid`: keep non-matching literal entries in the result instead of dropping them

"dynamic_expand_pairlist(config: dict[str, Any], markets: list[str]) -> pairlist:list[str]":
  location: pairlist_helpers.py
  annotations: |
    `expand_pairlist` over the configured pairs, additionally including any FreqAI
    correlation-pairlist pairs when FreqAI is enabled in `config`.

